armland-atlas/north-dakota/slope-county"],["ARC or PLC in Slope County","/arc-plc/north-dakota/slope-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids in Slope County came in under 90% of normal in September to October 43 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran wet late, with October to November at 168% and November to December at 186% of normal. So far in 2026 it has run short, with February to March at 45% and May to June at 54% of normal. Every grid listed had its driest year in 1988, and grid 31604 fell to 45% that year.</p>"}
